2. **Make the plan visible, then proceed within scope.** Build the concrete `EXEC_PLAN`. Use `enter_plan_mode` / `exit_plan_mode` only when a material decision remains unresolved; otherwise present the plan in commentary and continue without another approval gate. Invoking this executor authorizes ordinary in-scope implementation and light validation.
3. **Delegate what benefits from it.** For bounded independent work, dispatch `agent` with `subagent_type: general-purpose` for implementation or `Explore` for read-only orientation. A configured tier model selects the matching named `agent` (`star-plan`, `star-exec`, or `star-read`) described above; never pass the raw value as a per-call model. The main agent owns integration and verified checks.
